{"id":"2da0ab1e-e6fa-46e5-ac3e-46b40b7c5f65","question":"How should Cloudflare Pages serve the salon app?","answer":"Use Pages for the static frontend and a same-origin Pages Function proxy for /api/* to the existing HTTPS Node backend. Keep the backend origin in the Cloudflare BACKEND_ORIGIN environment variable; do not embed credentials or the backend URL in client code. Cloudflare Pages must not be treated as a replacement for the Node/PostgreSQL backend, and the backend must be healthy before bookings or owner tools work.","timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:27:32.402Z","tags":["api","architecture","cloudflare","deployment","how","node","pages"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T14:27:32.402Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:27:32.456Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":["postgres","postgresql","cloudflare"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["api"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"EDUSE"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:27:31.947Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T14:27:32.479Z"}
{"id":"820541e5-5122-4d82-b752-8d3866aef9bc","question":"Why does the Pages proxy preserve streamed request bodies?","answer":"The Cloudflare Pages API proxy forwards request bodies and cookies, including the owner's multipart video upload. Adding the Fetch duplex half option keeps streaming request forwarding valid in Node-based tests and standard runtimes without buffering the potentially large upload.","timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:32:49.646Z","tags":["api","cloudflare","node","pages","proxy","upload","why"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T14:32:49.646Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:32:49.665Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":["cloudflare"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["api","streaming"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"EDUSE","email":"eo657034@gmail.com"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:32:48.866Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T14:32:49.769Z"}
{"id":"367fed78-f548-4009-99f3-619d702aa39a","question":"How was the local environment and runtime robustness hardened?","answer":"Added a zero-dependency .env loader (lib/env.mjs) integrated into server.mjs, migrate.mjs, and API verification tools. Fixed a media play() promise rejection crash in css/gallery.ts and synchronized router navigation in css/router.ts. Verified with 56 unit tests, 44 frontend checks, and 19 project checks.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:00:03.076Z","tags":["api","environment","how","robustness","testing"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T05:00:03.076Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:00:03.078Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":[],"patterns":[],"concepts":["api"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"eo657034-debug","email":"eo657034@gmail.com"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:00:02.999Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T05:00:03.094Z"}
{"id":"0c5ee859-ca93-4557-b3a7-d66dca3bc36a","question":"What errors remain in the wangui-beauty-bar project after a full read and verification run?","answer":"All automated checks pass (tsc --noEmit, 56 unit tests, 44 frontend checks, 19 project checks), so remaining defects are ones the suite cannot see. Highest-severity confirmed defect: server.mjs assertSameOrigin compares the Origin header host to req.headers.host, but behind the Cloudflare Pages proxy the forwarded Origin is the Pages domain while Host is the Render backend domain, so every owner mutation (sign-in, upload, PATCH, DELETE) returns 403 Cross-origin in the intended deployment. Verified by probe: same-origin 200, pages.dev origin vs backend host 403. Other findings: migrate.mjs never calls process.exit(1) so 'npm run migrate && node server.mjs' starts a server against an un-migrated DB (relying on the schema gate to exit 1); owner delete has no rollback if storage delete fails after unpublish; clientIp trusts socket address so all Pages traffic shares one rate-limit bucket; readJsonBody is duplicated between server.mjs and lib/http.mjs; serveStatic returns 404 instead of 400 on malformed percent-encoding; DECK: render.yaml startCommand and healthCheckPath, and the live Render backend /api/health timed out.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:23:33.779Z","tags":["api","audit","defects","deployment","node","security","verification"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T05:23:33.779Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:23:33.812Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":["rust","cloudflare"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["api","schema","storage"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"eo657034-debug","email":"eo657034@gmail.com"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:23:33.638Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T05:23:33.926Z"}
{"id":"c53ab47c-0398-41d3-8e9a-b948f367ada3","question":"How were the Pages-proxy 403 and the migration exit-code defects fixed?","answer":"Fixed both. (1) Extracted cross-site protection into lib/origin.mjs with assertSameOrigin(req, allowedOrigins) and parseAllowedOrigins(). The old check compared the Origin host to req.headers.host, which is always different behind the Cloudflare Pages proxy, so owner sign-in/upload/PATCH/DELETE returned 403. The new check keeps Sec-Fetch-Site cross-site rejection, trusts the request's own host, and additionally trusts origins from a new SITE_URL env var (comma-separated, normalized). server.mjs now imports it and passes ALLOWED_ORIGINS to all five call sites; added SITE_URL to .env.example and render.yaml and documented it in README. (2) migrate.mjs catch block now sets process.exitCode = 1 so 'npm run migrate && node server.mjs' stops instead of starting against an un-migrated DB; verified exit code 1 with bad credentials. Added test/origin.test.mjs (11 unit tests plus a DB-gated live server test that skips without DATABASE_URL/PGPASSWORD). Also removed the duplicated readJsonBody/clientIp from server.mjs and imported them from lib/http.mjs. Verified: tsc 0, 67/68 tests pass with 1 skip, frontend 44/44, project 19/19.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:30:51.732Z","tags":["api","bugfix","deployment","how","migration","node","security","validation"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T05:30:51.732Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:30:51.734Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":["rust","cloudflare"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["migration","database"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"eo657034-debug","email":"eo657034@gmail.com"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:30:51.612Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T05:30:51.750Z"}
{"id":"2e2caafc-31de-4663-a14b-8b5fc7d8865a","question":"How were the remaining audit findings fixed (delete rollback, rate-limit keying, static 500, catalogue shape)?","answer":"Fixed all four. (1) lib/owner-videos.mjs delete() now selects the previous published flag, unpublishes, and on storage-delete failure restores the original flag before rethrowing, so a failed delete no longer leaves a permanently hidden, undeletable row; rollback failure is logged as owner.video_delete_rollback_failed. (2) lib/http.mjs clientIp() now honors X-Forwarded-For only when the immediate peer is listed in a new TRUSTED_PROXIES env var, and normalizes ::ffff: IPv4-mapped addresses, so rate limits are keyed per customer instead of per proxy; a direct client spoofing the header is ignored. (3) lib/static.mjs wraps decodeURIComponent in try/catch and returns 400 instead of a 500 for malformed escapes like /video/%ZZ. (4) VideoCatalogue.load() normalizes bundled entries to published/priceKes/reviewRequired booleans so bundled and owner rows share one shape. Added TRUSTED_PROXIES to .env.example and render.yaml and documented it in README. New tests: test/hardening.test.mjs (9) and test/client-ip.test.mjs (9). Updated two pre-existing tests in test/owner-videos.test.mjs whose assertions encoded the old behavior (undefined published, fake pool lacking the published column, and positional at(-2)/at(-1) call assertions). Verified: tsc 0, 85/86 tests pass with 1 DB-gated skip, frontend 44/44, project 19/19.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:45:25.253Z","tags":["api","audit","bugfix","hardening","how","security","validation"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"source":"cli","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T05:45:25.252Z","result":"orphan"},"status":"active"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:45:25.254Z","action":"created"}],"entities":{"technologies":["rust","rest"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["storage","audit"]},"provenance":{"author":{"name":"eo657034-debug","email":"eo657034@gmail.com"},"source":"cli","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:45:25.165Z"},"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T05:45:25.267Z"}
{"id":"1793171723997-ig8za9","question":"Why is TRUSTED_PROXIES parsed when clientIp runs rather than at module import?","answer":"The server loads .env in its entrypoint, but ES module dependencies are evaluated before that module body executes. Parsing TRUSTED_PROXIES once at import time therefore ignored .env values. clientIp now parses the setting at call time, preserving trusted-proxy checks while honoring the loaded configuration; a regression test covers environment changes after module import. This complements the existing trusted-proxy rate-limit design per decision 2e2caafc-31de-4663-a14b-8b5fc7d8865a.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T07:15:23.997Z","tags":["bugfix","environment","local","rate-limit","render"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"status":"active","source":"agent-mcp","client":"copilot-cli","trust":"unreviewed","entities":{"technologies":["rust"],"patterns":[],"concepts":[],"tools":[]},"domain":"software"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T07:15:24.573Z","action":"created"}],"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T07:15:24.613Z"}
{"id":"1793171723997-ig8za9","question":"Why is TRUSTED_PROXIES parsed when clientIp runs rather than at module import?","answer":"The server loads .env in its entrypoint, but ES module dependencies are evaluated before that module body executes. Parsing TRUSTED_PROXIES once at import time therefore ignored .env values. clientIp now parses the setting at call time, preserving trusted-proxy checks while honoring the loaded configuration; a regression test covers environment changes after module import. This complements the existing trusted-proxy rate-limit design per decision 2e2caafc-31de-4663-a14b-8b5fc7d8865a.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T07:15:23.997Z","tags":["bugfix","environment","local","rate-limit","render"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"medium","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"status":"active","source":"agent-mcp","client":"copilot-cli","trust":"unreviewed","entities":{"technologies":["rust"],"patterns":[],"concepts":[],"tools":[]},"domain":"software","autoLink":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T07:15:25.060Z","result":"orphan"}},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T07:15:24.573Z","action":"created"}],"rev":2,"ts":"2026-10-28T07:15:25.070Z"}
