{"id":"1793185589872-6tr5bf","question":"How is the production Render Blueprint documented and what does it not certify?","answer":"README now documents how to select render.production.yaml, configure Supabase owner publishing and verified proxy addresses, review Render costs/backups, and conduct non-production validation. It states explicitly that infrastructure configuration is not proof of go-live readiness and lists unresolved operating/product gates: WhatsApp request monitoring, approved business details and privacy/retention, and absent staff booking management, automated notifications, payment, and customer self-service. The staging Blueprint remains separate.","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:06:29.872Z","tags":["deployment","operations","production","readiness","render"],"files":[],"status":"active","priority":"high","relationships":{"supersedes":[],"supersededBy":[],"relatedTo":[],"causes":[],"causedBy":[]},"metadata":{"status":"active","source":"agent-mcp","client":"Visual Studio Code","trust":"unreviewed","entities":{"technologies":["go","supabase"],"patterns":[],"concepts":["monitoring"],"tools":[]},"domain":"software"},"commitHashes":[],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:06:30.380Z","action":"created"}],"rev":1,"ts":"2026-10-28T11:06:30.394Z"}
